    // Atomic operations are implemented at the hardware level, allowing them to be executed in a single instruction cycle. This means that when multiple threads attempt to perform an atomic operation on the same variable, the GPU can manage these requests efficiently without the need for additional synchronization mechanisms like barriers. The hardware ensures that each atomic operation is completed fully before another thread can access the same variable, preventing

